# nr-office-comrs-excel-edit: the workbook editor of mixdog-office-com (src/excel/edit/{mod,values,sheets,styles,structure,drawings,charts,data,view,print}.rs,
# tests/excel_edit.rs, tests/excel_edit_live.rs, recorder/scenarios/excel-edit.json).
# Nothing was compiled (the lead builds the wave). No protocol row, no service, no SERVICE_PENDING name, no new dependency and no Cargo.lock line belong to this task:
# the crate already depends on regex, which the editor uses; every other import is the crate's own.

## 1. native/core/crates/mixdog-office-com/src/lib.rs (not owned by this task)
`pub mod excel;` is already asked for by nr-office-comrs-excel-read.wire (item 1); apply it once.

## 2. native/core/crates/mixdog-office-com/src/excel/mod.rs (owned by nr-office-comrs-excel-read, finished)
The module of the editor must be public so that tests/excel_edit.rs and tests/excel_edit_live.rs (separate crates) can build the editor. Replace

    pub(crate) mod edit;

by

    pub mod edit;

(`excel::edit::Editor` is the only public item; the operation modules inside stay private, except `charts`, see item 6.)

## 3. native/core/crates/mixdog-office-com/src/drivers.rs (not owned by this task)
In the `EDITORS` table add the line:

    ("xlsx", &crate::excel::edit::Editor),

## 4. native/core/crates/mixdog-office-com/Cargo.toml (not owned by this task)
Test targets, after `[[test]] name = "excel_read_live"` (or after `actions_live` where that one is not there yet):

    [[test]]
    name = "excel_edit"
    path = "tests/excel_edit.rs"

    [[test]]
    name = "excel_edit_live"
    path = "tests/excel_edit_live.rs"

## 5. tests/fixtures/MANIFEST.json (written by the recorder, not by hand)
`node recorder/record-office-com.mjs --area excel-edit` on the migration PC writes tests/fixtures/excel-edit/<scenario>.json and the manifest entries (area "excel-edit").
tests/excel_edit.rs lists them and reads them (`every_recorded_excel_edit_fixture_is_listed_and_readable`); until the recording exists the manifest lists none.

## 6. What the PowerPoint editor (nr-office-comrs-ppt-edit) may share with this one
`src/excel/edit/charts.rs` is declared `pub(crate) mod charts;` and holds three helpers that `office-com-host.ps1` shares between Excel and PowerPoint charts:
`chart_type_code` (Office-ChartTypeCode), `set_chart_title_face` (Set-ChartTitleFace) and `ink_on_fill` (Ink-OnFill), all `pub(crate)`.
If the PowerPoint editor has written its own copies, delete one set when the two are merged: the script has one of each.
